PATCH 155: FUN_0000_e459 -- the mission LOADING-screen setup (first blocker of the ACCEPT cascade).

e459 sets up + titles the "LOADING" screen (the first thing the BATTLES->OK->ACCEPT mission-start
cascade FUN_0000_e87a runs after the briefing).  Two asm-verified Ghidra defects (vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin
0xe459..0xe4b8), both SIGSEGV on the wild small-pointer deref:
  (a) e465-e481 the LOADING resource-load device methods `call [DGROUP:0x560/0x564/0x5b0]` with
      ax=name-index 0x1c ("LOADING.MRL"), cx=ds, bx=descriptor DGROUP:0xf6d4 -- the __allregs vector
      sites DROPPED ax/cx/bx, so the driver built a garbage filename from a stale name index.  Thread
      them exactly as the proven menu-bg loader e3f8 (patch 110/094) and the settings loader (17314):
      c560(0x1c,0x1c00,0xf6d4); c564(0x1c00,&desc); c5b0(4,word[desc]) (+ g_mga_fade_es like 17314).
  (b) e494-e499 the centered LOADING-title string index: `movzx bx,byte[DGROUP:0xf75f];
      mov si,word[DGROUP:(bx-0x8a0)]` -- Ghidra collapsed it to `word[(value@0xf75f)-0x8a0]` host-deref.
      si is a STRSEG offset (a358/a370 already rebase via DGROUP:0x70); recover bx as the byte value and
      si = word[DGROUP:(uint16)(bx-0x8a0)].
Verified via the throwaway ACCEPT-cascade trace: with e459 fixed, the cascade opens LOADING.MS3 then
LOADING.MRL -- the exact first two mission assets DOSBox opens (tools/oracle/trace_click3.sh) -- crash-free
through e459.  e459 is reached ONLY by the ACCEPT mission cascade (not yet wired into a verify flow), so
this is behaviour-neutral for the 19 covered flows.

